{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/routing/global-error-component","title":"Global error component","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"global-error-component","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Global error component"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"One component, declared once, for every failure a route decided not to handle"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"locally."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Use it when"}]},{"t":"text","text":" several exception codes deserve the same screen, or as the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"backstop for unexpected errors."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Not when"}]},{"t":"text","text":" a specific failure needs its own UI — "},{"t":"code","text":"renderComponent(...)"},{"t":"text","text":" in the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"route's handler is more precise. See"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/routing/exception-handling","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Route exception handling"}]},{"t":"text","text":"."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"When a route exception handler delegates to "},{"t":"code","text":"globalError()"},{"t":"text","text":", the outlet renders one"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"application-wide error component and feeds it the exception. That component can read "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"all"}]},{"t":"text","text":" of its"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"possible exceptions — typed and exhaustive — because the codes routed to it are mirrored in a global"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"registry maintained automatically by ESLint."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"register-the-component","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Register the component"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Pass "},{"